                       Generate pyproject.toml configuration from the\n                        provided CLI arguments and exit\n  --ignore-pyproject    Ignore pyproject.toml configuration\n  --install-skill {codex,claude-code}\n                        Install the bundled datamodel-code-generator Agent\n                        Skill and exit (experimental). Use --skill-scope to\n                        select a project or personal installation.\n  --job NAME            Run a named job from pyproject.toml [tool.datamodel-\n                        codegen.jobs.<name>] (experimental). Can be repeated.\n  --list-deprecations [{table,json,markdown}]\n                        List registered deprecations and scheduled breaking\n                        changes, then exit.\n  --list-experimental [{table,json,markdown}]\n                        List registered experimental features and their\n                        compatibility notes, then exit.\n  --no-color            disable colorized output\n  --output-format {text,json}\n                        Format for command output (default: text). Use json\n                        for structured output when supported.\n  --output-format-json-schema {config,generate-prompt,generation,model-metadata,structured-output}\n                        Output JSON Schema for the selected JSON output or\n                        JSON configuration format and exit.\n  --overwrite-skill     Replace an existing regular skill directory when used\n                        with --install-skill.\n  --profile PROFILE     Use a named profile from pyproject.toml\n                        [tool.datamodel-codegen.profiles.<name>]\n  --skill-scope {project,user}\n                        Installation scope for --install-skill (default:\n                        project). Project installs use .agents/skills or\n                        .claude/skills; user installs use the matching home\n                        directory.\n  --version             show version\n  